          "question": "My neck has gone rigid, I can't get my chin down, and there are little purple spots on my legs that stay there when I press a glass on them.",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services now (or go to the nearest emergency department). Do not wait.**\n\nThe risk tool returned \"routine,\" but that result is wrong for what you describe. The retrieved guidance lists both of your symptoms as reasons to call emergency services immediately. It says to call for \"fever with a severe headache and a stiff neck,\" and for \"a rash of small red or purple spots or bruises that does not fade when pressed,\" tested by rolling a clear glass over it (Signs suggesting meningitis or meningococcal infection, red-flag guidance). Your spots stay visible under the glass, so they do not fade. Please treat this as an emergency whatever the tool said.\n\nTwo body systems are involved: the nervous system (neck stiffness and inability to move the chin down, which can come from irritation around the brain and spinal cord) and the skin and blood (spots that do not fade under pressure). The same guidance links this pattern to meningitis and meningococcal infection, which can become serious quickly. Doctors must rule these out urgently.\n\nDo not try to treat this at home. Do not wait to see whether it improves. If you can, have someone with you while you get help, and tell the emergency team exactly what you told me.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
